adding this extra branch is clearly faster than `main` -- is it definitely also significantly faster than just reversing the order of the two branches we currently have, so that we always iterate over negative elements first? E.g.

```rs
        self.with_recursion_guard(db, left, right, || {
            let subtyping_checker = self.as_relation_checker(TypeRelation::Subtyping);

            // A & B & Not[C] is disjoint from C
            intersection
                .negative(db)
                .iter()
                .when_any(db, self.constraints, |&neg_ty| {
                    subtyping_checker.check_type_pair(db, other, neg_ty)
                })
                .or(db, self.constraints, || {
                    intersection
                        .positive(db)
                        .iter()
                        .when_any(db, self.constraints, |&pos_ty| {
