body:
This information is already available [via the completion context's cursor](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/blob/ddacf1547b9a16022b4f34e7a7efa995a6072178/crates/ty_ide/src/completion.rs#L901-L902), so I think we should avoid constructing it again. There's precedent for adding utility functions to the `ContextCursor` struct, so perhaps instead we add another such utility e.g.:

```rs
  impl<'m> ContextCursor<'m> {
      /// Returns the subscript whose complete slice is this string.
      fn subscript_for_string(
          &self,
          string_expr: &ast::ExprStringLiteral,
      ) -> Option<&'m ast::ExprSubscript> {
          let parent = self
              .covering_node
              .ancestors()
              .skip_while(|node| {
                  !matches!(
                      node,
                      ast::AnyNodeRef::ExprStringLiteral(expr)
                          if expr.range() == string_expr.range()
                  )
              })
              .nth(1)?;

          let ast::AnyNodeRef::ExprSubscript(subscript) = parent else {
              return None;
          };

          (subscript.slice.range() == string_expr.range()).then_some(subscript)
      }
  }
```

Then you can pass that value down from `add_string_literal_completions` and use it to adjust when you call `dictionary_initializer_keys`.

