body:
Nit: Is the fast-path here justified. I see how it avoids the allocation if `path` isn't a directory, but it also duplicates a couple of lines of code. 

It also makes the distinction between `ModulePath` and `ModuleDirectory` less clear to me. Now, `ModulePath` does not represent a valid module, it now points to an arbitrary directory. 

Codex suggests that we could also remove this optimization, and simplify the calling method to

```rust
if matches!(kind, FileType::Directory | FileType::Symlink)
    && is_identifier(name)
{
    names.insert(name.to_owned());
}
```

> The tradeoff is conservative false positives: a dangling symlink gets included, so the full resolver runs and discovers there are no descendants. Ordinary file-only names still benefit from skipping that search.

Which seems a fine enough trade off to me

