body:
I personally find `map_or_else` hard to read, so I'd lean towards using `.map(Ok).or_else(...)` here. Happily, in this situation that's also 3 lines less code:

```suggestion
                let comparison = literal_membership.map(Ok).unwrap_or_else(|| {
                    comparisons::infer_binary_type_comparison(
                        &builder.context,
                        left_ty,
                        *op,
                        right_ty,
                        range,
                    )
                });
```

But TBH, the clearest of all here might be an explicit `match`? The conversion here is sort-of complex

```suggestion
                let comparison = match literal_membership {
                    Some(ty) => Ok(ty),
                    None => comparisons::infer_binary_type_comparison(
                        &builder.context,
                        left_ty,
                        *op,
                        right_ty,
                        range,
                    ),
                };
```

