body:
Reading `resolve_child` here followed by `enter_package`, it makes me wonder if it would be clearer to have a single `child(&component_name)` method that returns `Option<Child>` and `Child` is a `Module` or a `Package`. You can enter a `package`, or convert to a `Child`, but not more.


Edit: Codex thinks that `Module` vs `Package` does not work but it suggests something like:

```rust
enum Child {
    Leaf(Module),
    Prefix(PrefixChild),
}

impl PrefixChild {
    fn module(&self) -> Option<Module>;

    // Constructs the descendant search state on demand.
    fn enter(self) -> Option<ModuleSearchCursor>;
}
```

I don't think it's very important, given that most of this is internal. But there's some overlap between `resolve_child` and `enter_package` (which resolves whether it is a package)

