body:
same comment here -- can we make the type variables class-scoped instead of function-scoped? That way there are plausible solutions to the type variable other than `Unknown`, and it's more obvious why you might use a type variable in the first place. Or does it then cease to test what you're trying to test?

```suggestion
from typing import Protocol

class GenericSetter[T]:
    @property
    def value(self) -> object:
        return None

    @value.setter
    def value(self, value: T) -> None: ...

class BoundedSetter[I: int]:
    @property
    def value(self) -> object:
        return None

    @value.setter
    def value(self, value: I) -> None: ...

class HasValue(Protocol):
    value: object

def check(generic: GenericSetter, bounded: BoundedSetter, value: object) -> None:
    generic.value = value
    writable: HasValue = generic
    bounded.value = 1
    bounded.value = value  # error: [invalid-assignment]
    writable = bounded  # error: [invalid-assignment]
```

the type-variable uses here are a bit meaningless -- these type variables can only ever be solved to `Unknown` because of the fact that each only appears once in its respective signature, so it's very unclear why you'd use type variables like this. Can we make the example more realistic? Would this still test what you're trying to test here?

```suggestion
from typing import Protocol, TypeVar, Generic

T = TypeVar("T")
I = TypeVar("I", bound=int)

class GenericSetter(Generic[T]):
    @property
    def value(self) -> object:
        return None

    @value.setter
    def value(self, value: T) -> None: ...

class BoundedSetter(Generic[I]):
    @property
    def value(self) -> object:
        return None

    @value.setter
    def value(self, value: I) -> None: ...

class HasValue(Protocol):
    value: object

def check(generic: GenericSetter, bounded: BoundedSetter, value: object) -> None:
    generic.value = value
    writable: HasValue = generic
    bounded.value = 1
    bounded.value = value  # error: [invalid-assignment]
    writable = bounded  # error: [invalid-assignment]
```

