body:
Could we keep checking property accessors when their exposed types are wrappers or `Callable`s? This now passes, whereas `main` reports `invalid-generic-class`:

```python
from functools import cache
from typing import Generic, TypeVar

T_contra = TypeVar("T_contra", contravariant=True)

class C(Generic[T_contra]):
    @property
    @cache
    def value(self) -> T_contra:
        raise NotImplementedError
```

The property still produces `T_contra`, but `local_functions_from_type` cannot recover a function from the cache wrapper, so we skip the accessor entirely. I get the same regression with a signature-preserving `Callable[P, R]` decorator, on both getters and setters.

Could we recover the source metadata separately from the exposed accessor type, and check the latter even when it is no longer a `FunctionType`? Falling back to checking the original signature would miss decorators that change variance requirements.

